hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23597","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid, meaning Ibn Jabir, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aish, from some of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to them one morning cheerful, bright of face, or radiant of face. Then we said: O Messenger of Allah, we see you cheerful, bright of face, or radiant of face. Then he said: What prevents me, when my Lord came to me tonight in the best form and said: O Muhammad. I said: Here I am, my Lord, at Your service. Then He said: In what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: I do not know, my Lord. He said that two or three times. He said: Then He placed His palm between my shoulders, and I felt its coolness between my breasts, until all that is in the heavens and the earth manifested to me. Then he recited this verse: And thus We show Ibrahim the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, the verse. He said: O Muhammad, in what does the highest assembly dispute? He said: I said: In expiations. He said: And what are expiations? I said: Walking on feet to congregations, and sitting in mosques after prayers, and completing ablution in hardships. Whoever does that lives well and dies well and is from his sin like the day his mother bore him. And among ranks are: good speech, and spreading peace, and feeding food, and praying at night while people sleep. Then He said: O Muhammad, when you pray, say: O Allah, I ask You for good deeds, and leaving evils, and love of the poor, and that You turn to me; and when You intend a trial among people, take me to You un-tried."
"23598","Al-Zubayri Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Simak, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Amir narrated to me; one who heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to me, and he ordered the stoning of a man between Makkah and Madinah, and when he felt the touch of the stones, he went out and fled. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Why did you not leave him?"
"23599","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from a man, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you made a prophet? He said: While Adam was between spirit and body."
